  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The grotto-heaven is deserted and absolutely empty, with a lemon-like yellow color dyeing the air slightly. It is devoid of mountains, vegetation, and animals.",
      "chapters": [
        466
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "At Lang Ya Blessed Land, the land spirit recalls seeing a swarm of starlight fireflies during a transaction in treasure yellow heaven and attributes that swarm to Star Lord Wan Xiang. Fang Yuan seeks connecting heaven Gu and divine sense Gu so he can impersonate a Gu Immortal and trade there for resources.",
      "chapters": [
        462
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_lang_ya_blessed_land",
        "char_star_lord_wan_xiang",
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "sys_gu_immortal"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The land spirit later says a refined stargate Gu could be put in treasure yellow heaven to sell.",
      "chapters": [
        463
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Deviation (recorded): this page uses the Northern Plains region field because chapter 462 first names the market during talk inside Lang Ya blessed land. The novel does not give treasure yellow heaven a five-region map seat.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "reg_northern_plains"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Through connecting heaven Gu from Hu Immortal Blessed Land, the mirror shows a deserted grotto-heaven with lemon-like yellow air and no mountains, vegetation, or animals. It is closely related to yellow heaven among the immemorial nine heavens. In the Medieval Antiquity Era, a rank eight Gu Immortal known as Daoist Countless Treasures fused a yellow heaven fragment into his grotto-heaven and formed treasure yellow heaven. It holds only precious goods, and a rank eight Immortal Gu, treasure light Gu, sits inside; that Gu assesses value by brightness of light and can also search for treasure. Treasure light Gu at rank one to three are common, rank four to five often sit with large forces, and the Immortal Gu above rank five is unique to treasure yellow heaven.",
      "chapters": [
        466
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "grotto-heaven-and-treasure-light",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_hu_immortal_blessed_land",
        "loc_immemorial_nine_heavens",
        "evt_era_medieval",
        "char_daoist_countless_treasures",
        "sys_immortal_gu",
        "gu_treasure_light_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treasure yellow heaven is the greatest transaction market among Gu Immortals, and Immortal Gu sales there are very rare. Gu Immortals browse and bargain by divine sense while goods pass through connecting heaven Gu.",
      "chapters": [
        467
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "trade-practice",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Transactions depend heavily on treasure light: stronger light raises the price, and when the light weakens the sale price falls. The market takes a processing fee on trades. Immortal essence stones can serve as currency, yet most deals still use barter. Treasure light height alone cannot prove a Gu worm is untampered, so buyers may still refine for safety.",
      "chapters": [
        469
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "trade-practice",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_immortal_essence_stone",
        "sys_gu_worms"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "A blessed land’s owner can keep an ownership-recognition request open in treasure yellow heaven to make outsiders believe the land is unclaimed; Fang Yuan uses this to hide that he owns Star Form blessed land.",
      "chapters": [
        852
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "owner-masks-blessed-land-status",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "loc_star_form_blessed_land"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan judges that his personally devised star night mucus would sell as a monopoly in treasure yellow heaven, fetching a good price.",
      "chapters": [
        931
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "a-personal-monopoly",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "A quasi-rank nine immortal material is precious enough that it would create a huge commotion in treasure yellow heaven and sell without trouble.",
      "chapters": [
        936
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "precious-enough-to-guarantee-a-sale",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan puts up only the lowest-quality rank eight immortal materials of his inventory, and even that creates waves of commotion there, since rank eight materials draw huge attraction.",
      "chapters": [
        952
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "even-low-grade-stock-draws-a-crowd",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Treasure yellow heaven also serves as a path for moving Gu worms. It is an open market rather than a secret channel, which makes it unsafe for a transfer meant to stay hidden.",
      "chapters": [
        1032
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "a-path-for-moving-gu-worms",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its opening and closing is an event in the Gu Immortal world.",
      "chapters": [
        1073
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "opening-and-closing",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "After becoming owner of Liu Qing Yu’s blessed land, Fang Yuan orders its duck land spirit that if any enemies attack, it must inform him through treasure yellow heaven immediately.",
      "chapters": [
        1152
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "emergency-signal",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_qing_yu_blessed_land"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Listings there accrue fees the longer they sit unsold, so Fang Yuan retrieves two desolate beast corpses that draw no buyers rather than keep paying to list them.",
      "chapters": [
        1177
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "fees-for-unsold-listings",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "A seller may leave a will there to look after unsold goods; the will can think and converse but must hold strictly to the bottom-line price its main body set, so real negotiation needs the main body’s own divine sense to join in.",
      "chapters": [
        1314
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "a-wills-price-floor",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Treasure yellow heaven’s business includes information transactions: methods for countering Gu worms, introductions to and understandings of Gu paths, news of the present political situation, and deductions by time path and wisdom path Gu Immortals on the past, present and future. Fang Yuan buys a set of The Encyclopedia of Earth Path Gu Worms there from an earth path Gu Immortal, along with other relevant information that includes mortal formation path inheritances, paying close to ten immortal essence stones for all of it. Fang Yuan’s five hundred years of past experience could supply information certain to draw buyers, but he has never considered selling any of it, since such information normally goes cheap and parting with it would weaken his rebirth advantage.",
      "chapters": [
        1324
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "information-trade",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "path_earth"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Heavenly Court has the means to watch the place, and because any transaction in an open market is exposed easily, Fairy Zi Wei must know that Fang Yuan borrowed Immortal Gu and immortal essence stones from Wu clan through it.",
      "chapters": [
        1370
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "an-open-market-under-watch",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_heavenly_court",
        "char_fairy_zi_wei",
        "fac_wu_clan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan puts a portion of his newly bred copper dragonfish up for sale there.",
      "chapters": [
        1477
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "copper-dragonfish-goes-to-market",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Treasure yellow heaven is safe enough that even Heavenly Court has no options against it, so the Gu Immortal experts who want Fang Yuan’s food path true inheritance approach his will there instead of reaching him directly.",
      "chapters": [
        1478
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "a-safe-place-to-approach-a-rival",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "You Chan’s dragonfish business is famous enough across all five regions that Qing Yue Zhi Cheng expects she keeps a will there to manage it, and he contacts that will while searching for her.",
      "chapters": [
        1488
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "you-chans-will-there",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_you_chan",
        "char_qing_yue_zhi_cheng"
      ]
    }
  ],
